        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sovereign immunity should not bar enforcement of the consent decree in this case for two reasons. First, when State officials ask a district court to enter a consent decree, they submit their rights concerning the decree for judicial determination, thereby waiving any possible claim for objection on the basis of immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: May I ask on -- on the first point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Texas' Attorney General is authorized by the legislature to represent the State and its employees --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Enforcement of the decree in this case does not violate the Eleventh Amendment for two reasons. First, any Eleventh Amendment objection was waived, and second, enforcement is permissible under Ex Parte Young."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In an Ex Parte Young action, State officials like all other Federal litigants are free to enter into consent decrees that go beyond what is strictly required by Federal law on one or more issues because there is a tradeoff."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I'm not worried about the officials."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By the way, the State also has the right always to move for modification of provisions under this Court's decision in Rufo that are not arguably related to -- that are not related to any arguable violation of Federal law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We argued extensively that we were carrying out our promises."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Some of the arguments made are not tethered in -- tethered or tied to the record in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There has been no contested motion to modify filed in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Would a change in administrations be a change of circumstances that -- that justifies 60(b) being invoked?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is there then a way to deal with the problem that Justice Scalia raised, which is a serious problem I think?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-628",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1da291b3f9a03d4ac99fc03f37b3a221e7430347bd7977de1b84cfb9268b6936",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1da291b3f9a0-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But it's a known problem, and what's your solution to it?"
    }
  ],
